# Cursor native evidence carrier

Cursor performs browser evidence with `cursor-ide-browser` and `browser_cdp` evaluation in the same interaction round. Native IDE interaction and the verified browser session provide the URL, DOM, and screenshot receipt; a status message alone is not evidence.

Cursor uses its native `Task` surface for separated work only when routing permits it. If a required browser, authenticated session, or command capability is unavailable in the current IDE session, keep the item blocked and preserve the fallback trail.
